Subject: [PATCH 0005] aerial-fh: change the transmit buffer's physical backing while the queue runs

Supersedes 0004, which proved the idea but could only set the alias factor at queue
creation, so every value cost an L1 restart. Measured then, on GH200 with the DU-High
attached: 26,146 -> 17,952 MiB at N=2, 8,194 MiB returned, DOCA registering the full
16 GiB in dmabuf mode and CRC staying at zero.

This makes the factor changeable on a live queue.

The virtual range is cut into FH_ALIAS_SLOTS (16) equal slots, each mapped onto one
physical handle. With N distinct handles slot k uses handle k % N, so N = 16 is full
backing and N = 1 leaves one slot's worth of memory behind the whole range.
Reshaping repoints slots one at a time and releases the handles that fall out of use.

DOCA still sees nothing: the base address, the length and the mkey are untouched and
the queue is never stopped. That is the point -- every setter in doca_eth_rxq.h is
documented "can only be called before calling doca_ctx_start()", so the obvious way
to resize costs a fronthaul outage.

Reshaping one slot at a time keeps the unmapped window to 1/16 of the range rather
than all of it. The window is nonetheless real: cuMemUnmap followed by cuMemMap
leaves that slot unmapped for a few microseconds, and a NIC write landing there in
that moment faults. This is why the reshape is driven by an explicit command instead
of happening on its own -- it is safe when the ring's write pointer is elsewhere, and
nothing here knows where that is yet. Reading the write pointer and reshaping behind
it is the obvious next step.

Control is a file poller:

    echo "alias 4" > /var/log/aerial/fh_ctl      results in fh_ctl.out

Crude on purpose. This is a harness, not the API; the real control path belongs on
the OAM gRPC service, off the real-time cores.

AERIAL_FH_ALIAS_N still sets the value at startup and still defaults to 1, which does
not enter this code at all, so the patch stays inert until asked for.

Compile-verified on 26-1-cubb. The runtime behaviour is untested: the reshape path
has never been executed. The first run of it is the experiment.

--- a/cuPHY-CP/aerial-fh-driver/lib/doca_obj.cpp
+++ b/cuPHY-CP/aerial-fh-driver/lib/doca_obj.cpp
@@ -20,6 +20,216 @@
 #include "gpu_comm.hpp"
 #include "aerial-fh-driver/api.hpp"
 #include "app_config.hpp"
+#include <cuda.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <thread>
+#include <chrono>
+#include <fstream>
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <string>
+
+/*
+ * NOTICE: modified from the NVIDIA Aerial CUDA-Accelerated RAN SDK 26-1-cubb.
+ * Change: AERIAL_FH_ALIAS_N backs the fronthaul transmit buffer with one physical
+ * allocation of size/N mapped N times across the full virtual range.
+ * Marked as required by Apache License 2.0 section 4(b).
+ */
+
+/*
+ * Back a buffer of `size` bytes with `size/n` bytes of physical memory, mapped n
+ * times across the full virtual range.
+ *
+ * The point is that DOCA and the NIC see no difference: same base address, same
+ * length, same mkey, and the queue never stops.  That matters because every setter
+ * in doca_eth_rxq.h is documented "can only be called before calling
+ * doca_ctx_start()", so resizing a buffer the obvious way means a fronthaul outage.
+ * Aliasing changes only what sits behind the addresses.
+ *
+ * Correctness needs the alias period to exceed the lifetime of a packet in the
+ * buffer.  On the transmit side that lifetime is microseconds (U-plane prepare
+ * ~13 us, transmit ~7 us measured), so the margin is large.
+ *
+ * n == 1 is the stock path and is not routed through here at all.
+ */
+/*
+ * Slot-based aliasing, reshapeable while the queue runs.
+ *
+ * The virtual range is cut into FH_ALIAS_SLOTS equal slots.  Each slot is mapped
+ * onto one physical handle.  With N distinct handles, slot k uses handle k % N, so
+ * N == SLOTS is full backing and N == 1 is one slot's worth of physical memory
+ * behind the whole range.
+ *
+ * Reshaping touches one slot at a time, so the window in which any address is
+ * unmapped covers 1/SLOTS of the range rather than all of it.  DOCA sees nothing:
+ * the base address, the length and the mkey are untouched and the queue is never
+ * stopped.
+ *
+ * The window is real, though.  cuMemUnmap followed by cuMemMap leaves that slot
+ * unmapped for a few microseconds, and a NIC write landing there in that moment
+ * faults.  Reshaping is therefore safe when the ring's write pointer is elsewhere,
+ * which is why this is driven by an explicit command rather than done automatically.
+ */
+static void fh_alias_start_ctl();
+
+#define FH_ALIAS_SLOTS 16
+
+struct FhAliasState {
+    CUdeviceptr                  va;                        /* base, never changes */
+    size_t                       slot;                      /* bytes per slot */
+    size_t                       total;                     /* slot * FH_ALIAS_SLOTS */
+    CUmemGenericAllocationHandle handle[FH_ALIAS_SLOTS];    /* owner handle per slot, 0 if aliased */
+    int                          backing[FH_ALIAS_SLOTS];   /* which slot's handle each slot uses */
+    int                          n;                         /* distinct handles in use */
+    bool                         live;
+};
+static FhAliasState g_fh_alias = {};
+
+static bool fh_alias_prop(CUmemAllocationProp *prop, size_t *gran)
+{
+    CUdevice dev = 0;
+    if(cuCtxGetDevice(&dev) != CUDA_SUCCESS) return false;
+    memset(prop, 0, sizeof(*prop));
+    prop->type          = CU_MEM_ALLOCATION_TYPE_PINNED;
+    prop->location.type = CU_MEM_LOCATION_TYPE_DEVICE;
+    prop->location.id   = (int)dev;
+    return cuMemGetAllocationGranularity(gran, prop, CU_MEM_ALLOC_GRANULARITY_MINIMUM) == CUDA_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+static bool fh_alias_map_slot(int k, int src)
+{
+    FhAliasState &st = g_fh_alias;
+    CUmemAllocationProp prop; size_t gran;
+    if(!fh_alias_prop(&prop, &gran)) return false;
+    CUdeviceptr at = st.va + (CUdeviceptr)k * st.slot;
+    if(cuMemMap(at, st.slot, 0, st.handle[src], 0) != CUDA_SUCCESS) return false;
+    CUmemAccessDesc acc; memset(&acc, 0, sizeof(acc));
+    acc.location = prop.location;
+    acc.flags    = CU_MEM_ACCESS_FLAGS_PROT_READWRITE;
+    if(cuMemSetAccess(at, st.slot, &acc, 1) != CUDA_SUCCESS) return false;
+    st.backing[k] = src;
+    return true;
+}
+
+/* Build the range with `n` distinct handles.  Called once, at queue creation. */
+static doca_error_t fh_alias_alloc(size_t size, int n, void **addr_out, size_t *phys_out)
+{
+    FhAliasState &st = g_fh_alias;
+    CUmemAllocationProp prop; size_t gran;
+    if(!fh_alias_prop(&prop, &gran)) return DOCA_ERROR_BAD_STATE;
+    if(n < 1) n = 1;
+    if(n > FH_ALIAS_SLOTS) n = FH_ALIAS_SLOTS;
+
+    st.slot  = (((size + FH_ALIAS_SLOTS - 1) / FH_ALIAS_SLOTS) + gran - 1) / gran * gran;
+    st.total = st.slot * FH_ALIAS_SLOTS;
+    if(cuMemAddressReserve(&st.va, st.total, gran, 0, 0) != CUDA_SUCCESS) return DOCA_ERROR_NO_MEMORY;
+
+    for(int k = 0; k < n; k++)
+        if(cuMemCreate(&st.handle[k], st.slot, &prop, 0) != CUDA_SUCCESS) return DOCA_ERROR_NO_MEMORY;
+    for(int k = 0; k < FH_ALIAS_SLOTS; k++)
+        if(!fh_alias_map_slot(k, k % n)) return DOCA_ERROR_BAD_STATE;
+
+    st.n    = n;
+    st.live = true;
+    *addr_out = (void *)st.va;
+    *phys_out = st.slot * (size_t)n;
+    fh_alias_start_ctl();
+    return DOCA_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Change the number of distinct handles while the queue runs.
+ * Shrinking aliases the surplus slots onto surviving handles and releases theirs;
+ * growing gives them handles of their own again.  Returns bytes now backing the
+ * range, or 0 on failure.
+ */
+static size_t fh_alias_reshape(int n)
+{
+    FhAliasState &st = g_fh_alias;
+    if(!st.live) return 0;
+    if(n < 1) n = 1;
+    if(n > FH_ALIAS_SLOTS) n = FH_ALIAS_SLOTS;
+    if(n == st.n) return st.slot * (size_t)st.n;
+
+    CUmemAllocationProp prop; size_t gran;
+    if(!fh_alias_prop(&prop, &gran)) return 0;
+
+    if(n > st.n)                       /* grow: give slots n-1..st.n their own memory */
+    {
+        for(int k = st.n; k < n; k++)
+        {
+            if(cuMemCreate(&st.handle[k], st.slot, &prop, 0) != CUDA_SUCCESS) return 0;
+            cuMemUnmap(st.va + (CUdeviceptr)k * st.slot, st.slot);
+            if(!fh_alias_map_slot(k, k)) return 0;
+        }
+    }
+    for(int k = 0; k < FH_ALIAS_SLOTS; k++)   /* repoint every slot at its new owner */
+    {
+        int want = k % n;
+        if(st.backing[k] == want) continue;
+        cuMemUnmap(st.va + (CUdeviceptr)k * st.slot, st.slot);
+        if(!fh_alias_map_slot(k, want)) return 0;
+    }
+    if(n < st.n)                       /* shrink: the surplus handles are now unreferenced */
+    {
+        for(int k = n; k < st.n; k++)
+        {
+            if(st.handle[k]) { cuMemRelease(st.handle[k]); st.handle[k] = 0; }
+        }
+    }
+    st.n = n;
+    return st.slot * (size_t)n;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Drive fh_alias_reshape from outside while the cell runs.  A file poller, which is
+ * crude on purpose: this is a test harness, not the API.  The real control path
+ * belongs on the OAM gRPC service, off the real-time cores.
+ *
+ *   echo "alias 4" > /var/log/aerial/fh_ctl      results appear in fh_ctl.out
+ */
+static void fh_alias_ctl_loop()
+{
+    const char *in  = "/var/log/aerial/fh_ctl";
+    const char *out = "/var/log/aerial/fh_ctl.out";
+
+    CUdevice  dev = 0;
+    CUcontext ctx = nullptr;
+    if(cuDeviceGet(&dev, 0) == CUDA_SUCCESS && cuDevicePrimaryCtxRetain(&ctx, dev) == CUDA_SUCCESS)
+        cuCtxSetCurrent(ctx);
+
+    for(;;)
+    {
+        std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(200));
+        std::string cmd; int n = 0;
+        {
+            std::ifstream f(in);
+            if(!f.good()) continue;
+            f >> cmd >> n;
+        }
+        std::remove(in);
+        if(cmd != "alias" || n <= 0) continue;
+
+        int    before = g_fh_alias.n;
+        size_t phys   = 0;
+        try { phys = fh_alias_reshape(n); } catch(...) { phys = 0; }
+
+        std::ofstream o(out, std::ios::app);
+        if(phys)
+            o << "alias " << before << " -> " << g_fh_alias.n << ": "
+              << (g_fh_alias.total >> 20) << " MiB virtual backed by " << (phys >> 20)
+              << " MiB physical" << std::endl;
+        else
+            o << "alias " << before << " -> " << n << ": FAILED" << std::endl;
+    }
+}
+
+static void fh_alias_start_ctl()
+{
+    static bool started = false;
+    if(started) return;
+    started = true;
+    std::thread(fh_alias_ctl_loop).detach();
+}
 
 
 #define GPU_PAGE_SHIFT 16
@@ -484,7 +694,23 @@
